Both files contain the same problematic code: (1) the `deoptional` type utility at line 1636 that only unwraps `ZodOptional` but not `ZodNullable`, and (2) the `.required()` method at lines 1988-1990 and 1998-2000 that only unwraps `ZodOptional` instances. When `.nullish()` returns `ZodNullable<ZodOptional<T>>`, the `.required()` call fails to remove the inner optional flag because it stops at the `ZodNullable` layer.
